Looking at the errors: the compiler does not recognize the `public` implementations of `getSObjectType()` / `getSObjectFieldList()` as overrides of the `fflib_SObjectSelector` abstract methods, while still demanding those abstract methods be implemented. That is the classic Apex signature/mismatch caused by a visibility mismatch (the base `fflib_` methods being `global`), which requires the implementing class and methods to be declared `global` as well. I've fixed the class accordingly, keeping everything else (defaults, single bulk-safe dynamic query, empty-set guard) intact.

